    "created_at": "2025-05-01T19:25:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-01T19:29:19Z",
    "body": "cc @DCtheTall @johannhof\n\nHey just wanted to follow up on this since there is more adoption of the API now and the cross-browser implementations are aligned on using `Strict` by default. \n\nWhile using `Lax` could help make the CookieStore API more interoperable with `document.cookie` or HTTP cookie defaults, \n- Making it truly interoperable would suggest `lax-allowing-unsafe` should be the default which is unideal\n- Changing the default from `Strict` to `Lax` could be a security sensitive change \n\nI think Chromium is okay with sticking to `Strict` by default unless @annevk or @bakulf have any reservations or preferences? \n\n(and @rowan-m we can definitely call this out in the spec if that would abate some developer confusion?)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
